  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:684",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the regulation of Diacylglycerol kinase alpha through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Theasaponin E1 acts as a target of K-252a, which in turn targets Diacylglycerol kinase alpha. This indicates a potential role for K-252a in mediating the effects of Theasaponin E1 on Diacylglycerol kinase alpha. Additionally, Theasaponin E1 is also shown to target another protein, Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which is subsequently targeted by K-252a. This suggests that Theasaponin E1 may influence Diacylglycerol kinase alpha through a series of molecular interactions involving K-252a and other proteins. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex network of interactions that may underlie the biological effects of Theasaponin E1, emphasizing the importance of K-252a as a central mediator in this relationship.",
